#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096394 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/id #uuid "f1021ccd-e37f-5880-baf2-0f0eacd7dd95" :question/math-academy-id "e-481" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x\t&= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos  \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right).\n  }\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( - \\cos {x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096395 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "99b7b82d-431f-5992-9b1e-a80a6b3850c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-482" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int ( \\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n                                                                 &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096396 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "6269e793-cee7-59d6-8656-12a5a7475f2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-483" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right )=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right )=\\sin^2(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096397 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/id #uuid "55a54d74-449e-5720-b808-9f275b678b2e" :question/math-academy-id "e-484" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab5f853a-f9f7-56d4-b9c4-e47e7bd74413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}\\sin 6x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093508} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b3aa65-7431-5061-9409-9c24fba84a50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\cos 6x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093509} {:answer/id #uuid "1be0d939-4554-5daa-bb6d-1d0544e257a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\sin 6x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093510} {:answer/id #uuid "39efbf03-3fcd-55d6-94d5-baa34a84f61e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}\\cos 6x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093511} {:answer/id #uuid "3f45b23d-b6ea-5650-a2f6-81b377b81572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\sin 6x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39efbf03-3fcd-55d6-94d5-baa34a84f61e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}\\cos 6x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093511} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4ef0f30-7ef6-552d-96f3-74e77975dc6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38cc180c-008e-58cf-9362-f626ff2e1428" :question/math-academy-id "q-10440" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41e225e4-2ee1-5814-a582-e6909c47e280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288655} {:answer/id #uuid "dac30b7c-f0b1-5d3a-9e2d-0068f819b118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288656} {:answer/id #uuid "110cffd9-5a80-5622-b762-451a6bea3517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288657} {:answer/id #uuid "2548ab99-eeff-5b0f-8013-ecbd30fee4f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288658} {:answer/id #uuid "6580d80e-f036-5373-be82-e21593775432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41e225e4-2ee1-5814-a582-e6909c47e280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288655} :answer-field/id #uuid "e12514f3-672a-524d-80c8-c4ad7465c258" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b4ce5cf0-789a-541d-8352-d0ab9f8317eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-114681" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{5x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5x}{2})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x]}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot [0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a105aec-230b-517f-841c-b2661bf2a900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288669} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e3b438-1c73-56ac-9412-4592de70d7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288670} {:answer/id #uuid "d59678ce-a185-53af-be9a-c8d960acb4b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288671} {:answer/id #uuid "29ef0955-b526-5552-b399-ffcbc9567878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288672} {:answer/id #uuid "9c382ece-6e51-56d8-bce3-c4235b81f26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29ef0955-b526-5552-b399-ffcbc9567878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288672} :answer-field/id #uuid "557b5326-0b9a-5ce6-9ba9-59bb1ceaac8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "11ec7c4e-aed1-52ff-98e9-641fb20ec61b" :question/math-academy-id "q-114688" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x={cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({sin}^{2}⁡4x-{cos}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "303fa97f-3d61-5184-a349-c12f8c8074bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303616} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe4ba27-02f7-5c91-9f48-1a56dab35618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303617} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b3d3e2-ebdd-5027-9f80-9ab86295e47c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303618} {:answer/id #uuid "9fae57e2-8599-5683-863f-a150d85259c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303619} {:answer/id #uuid "2ec8596c-f498-545c-ad50-8a9b0f32a482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fae57e2-8599-5683-863f-a150d85259c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303619} :answer-field/id #uuid "d65407ce-aa3d-565c-8639-4943b98cc9f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5e06f254-9ae0-5c9b-85c7-9e6e4070e958" :question/math-academy-id "q-114696" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\theta =x$ and substituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {(2{cos}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the same formula $2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1$ with $\\theta =2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\frac{3}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+\\frac{3}{2}\\,x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{3x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82a62c8c-484c-5495-b1b7-5f5850631915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303623} {:answer/id #uuid "e351c5e5-ab8b-59db-9b5e-19896b7eccad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303624} {:answer/id #uuid "c5db3896-3524-5c26-a73f-323d24950fa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303625} {:answer/id #uuid "c113ef7a-beb6-5603-95df-92ad4f197e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303626} {:answer/id #uuid "904d90a7-bfff-5e62-81a0-59241dac5e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}+x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e351c5e5-ab8b-59db-9b5e-19896b7eccad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303624} :answer-field/id #uuid "af6e7734-0646-5022-9cd7-6630c6f083fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4323046d-0eea-5be0-a5b7-ac027795bcc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-114706" :question/problem "$\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (2\\cdot 2{sin}^{2}⁡x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x-2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3{x}^{2}+C \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d43de327-f14f-5993-b86b-37f87c7eb6bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303630} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1ea649-8300-5c98-ab16-994898b76d4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303631} {:answer/id #uuid "8eeeb9d9-00a8-5f46-9313-37622780ab11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303632} {:answer/id #uuid "49cc67b2-e806-56cd-a818-e2d53cbf4609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303633} {:answer/id #uuid "c679b82c-12a6-5579-aa35-c0922a857353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c679b82c-12a6-5579-aa35-c0922a857353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303634} :answer-field/id #uuid "184b4d0f-01c1-54e3-9c60-6a883c5b3e9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4dc5f61-51e0-57b7-9717-0e7b5d819bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-114709" :question/problem "$\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c9c73e6-97df-51de-91dc-19edd1d6fc14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c9c73e6-97df-51de-91dc-19edd1d6fc14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303637} :answer-field/id #uuid "694ddeb6-b4bf-5f6e-8bbc-2bb046085ac3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ffc0ed13-441c-5653-8f7c-66f8bb3ae58b" :question/math-academy-id "q-347179" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/b163cd4cc1add41ae2c043b4b3d7d818dd9b23de0a4b762bc85d348c0bca4def.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\pi $ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2x)\\,|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot (-\\pi ))+2(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =(0+\\pi )-(0-2\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\pi +2\\pi  \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5dd8e22-4e53-5097-9663-141d62fb9e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5dd8e22-4e53-5097-9663-141d62fb9e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303640} :answer-field/id #uuid "d17d2d99-482a-5e96-a7f8-10615a206c45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7e6a604d-c591-56e2-a8f3-63cd2a5f1e21" :question/math-academy-id "q-347182" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )+\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3})-(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e35dce5-cd92-5b28-a495-352005bf7737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303643} {:answer/id #uuid "7f143a12-9050-5856-8db5-5ee5c6c21f43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e35dce5-cd92-5b28-a495-352005bf7737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303643} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcdb6414-d340-5241-913f-a7e0fdf66c27" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3b1100b1-bd62-51d2-8f07-e50972013e35" :question/math-academy-id "q-348715" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1e3f010-a779-5dc5-ba5e-a94c70cbde91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1e3f010-a779-5dc5-ba5e-a94c70cbde91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303647} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7d59754-0374-5e91-999c-69b88bd37a5d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e3198417-8b57-51db-a845-3bce4d1af637" :question/math-academy-id "q-348716" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/a2ccde221d71e611f7917d6dac0d12ca6b8204d9cd80a21d79005195245cf77a.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a6e0165-9d83-55fb-ae2d-479f4739eeb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288693} {:answer/id #uuid "ac39ac42-f4e3-514b-9b2e-99f867283e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a6e0165-9d83-55fb-ae2d-479f4739eeb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288693} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d5ffffe-5e70-56f4-9655-682fd848b6fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "255b135e-4c97-5cce-be01-da73a642bcfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-348719" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)={cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c2c9eba-cfb0-5554-be09-57e67e55798b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c2c9eba-cfb0-5554-be09-57e67e55798b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303650} :answer-field/id #uuid "4422bdb5-cfdd-5180-8ab9-8814273417ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "be9b4f41-fcc3-5951-9d3f-a279ae34a1a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-348723" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})={cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{3})\\,{|}_{-3\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b17ab2c0-a71e-5e7d-89c0-937a0a07f438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}+\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292525} {:answer/id #uuid "4027e753-7b1f-569d-b840-11bcfedf5934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}-\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4027e753-7b1f-569d-b840-11bcfedf5934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}-\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292526} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5efcb9-4aa5-5b02-9e9d-d93d68eb53f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59759616-b70c-500d-99c5-be22cfbb7cb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-348733" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+17x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{3}{2}(0)^{2}+17\\cdot 0]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{3}{2}{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+17(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =[0+0+0]-[0+\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}-\\frac{17\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =[0+\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303651 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a810f433-a2d7-5d74-8b19-05dd394c379b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a810f433-a2d7-5d74-8b19-05dd394c379b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303653} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e031aea-d803-5223-9c1c-8b78c0a5951b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34b4dfd3-f4cb-5193-b18f-933144f4071b" :question/math-academy-id "q-348845" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(8{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(8{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(4[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})]+4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2}(4-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})+4x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(4x-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2x}{5})+2{x}^{2})|}_{-5\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[4\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{2}-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2(5\\pi /2)}{5})+2{(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & \\,-[4\\cdot (-\\frac{5\\pi }{2})-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2(-5\\pi /2)}{5})+2{(-\\frac{5\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & =[10\\pi -10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+2(\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{4})]-[-10\\pi -10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )+2(\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{4})] \\\\  & =[10\\pi -0+\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{2}]-[-10\\pi -0+\\frac{25{\\pi }^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =20\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303654 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e70fdbe2-e3ff-5811-8b25-f2fe769c6def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi^3}{24}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e70fdbe2-e3ff-5811-8b25-f2fe769c6def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi^3}{24}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303656} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb12cd62-3c0e-552b-b36a-edaad2c59d0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3bdbba35-dcea-5023-a028-d70a659d314d" :question/math-academy-id "q-348886" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/d1d49c23cebfe2979c8bff7b7f19d5435807a8d1aec348070aadfab1e9d2ca19.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)=-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daa8bbfb-9cd5-5ac4-af5b-f95bc53fb68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303659} {:answer/id #uuid "97d09f74-cc14-5e81-92b4-2c27170d8852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daa8bbfb-9cd5-5ac4-af5b-f95bc53fb68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303659} :answer-field/id #uuid "311d916e-980e-58dc-aa9b-6dc55aa6720a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "33e4ffd8-e1ee-553a-bbc6-09f216ac15a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-348917" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/07a1fab6073fdff2a20140719b570c0c40981ab049866480fbaff4dfad0c7799.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x),$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))={sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{7}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}{(x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x))|}_{\\pi /4}^{5\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}[(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi ))-(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303661 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840e71bf-4b19-5f77-975a-504d60b8f831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303663} {:answer/id #uuid "cfdcdb89-1fa0-5e5b-a6dc-945460dab185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "840e71bf-4b19-5f77-975a-504d60b8f831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303663} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f2e647b-d35b-5008-bf4e-9afef43b2a41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aab9a792-b65b-5b10-9dcd-2375e14a55d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-361710" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x & =5{sin}^{2}⁡x+5{cos}^{2}⁡x+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[5+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(8+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(8x+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[8(0)+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0))] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}(0)]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}(0)] \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bf4c878-7b92-592b-adc2-112e45c4e87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303667} {:answer/id #uuid "60640a78-8f09-5331-a704-26677847ffbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60640a78-8f09-5331-a704-26677847ffbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303668} :answer-field/id #uuid "859cec6a-b48c-5542-b4bf-ce49ea1111b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5028512b-a5ef-5c38-81c4-6a7be0e32b0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-361711" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/f8aa97ff1ff27ec11df6aefd4523ed9d39efac686c777f7242701aa2f4fef79c.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2-x]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3-x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-[0] \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4c5541e-8195-53de-b604-e622c3b6a2e7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9158e8b-fd77-505c-ae95-b35316de8c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303671} {:answer/id #uuid "77f1fc74-be9a-5fe5-9b77-12855bceb06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303672} {:answer/id #uuid "14427c52-8bda-5e1d-9771-529c62678b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303673} {:answer/id #uuid "b58dc2d6-21ef-5bd3-b687-1966b9951d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303674} {:answer/id #uuid "add810f6-b96e-5e9b-8930-f4b0c9094e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9158e8b-fd77-505c-ae95-b35316de8c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303671} :answer-field/id #uuid "793b18b0-e232-509f-a3ab-fab10f91fc12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64089810-7ca1-537a-84e6-d34fa3690e9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74398" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aedd6cbe-175e-52fe-93d9-fe26d20f698c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303678} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a8cdb7-8b55-5fdf-9f62-8c60c698d08d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303679} {:answer/id #uuid "c5364b71-ef57-5d85-a9bf-4984ed0df16e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303680} {:answer/id #uuid "2872f309-90b9-5afd-b39b-1db06b2ed51c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303681} {:answer/id #uuid "09849ed7-3e2f-50fe-b708-f1b2736c5300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aedd6cbe-175e-52fe-93d9-fe26d20f698c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303678} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf09c7a-9d2a-5258-91ad-8a4c83e1c2e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b03e35a1-e734-50b6-bb4d-c119df26dd8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74402" :question/problem "$\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
